module nmd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.states.new-mexico.{ frcp6-new-mexico }

// The District of New Mexico's own civil periods, computed under the
// federal rules (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.4(a): the briefing periods "are computed
// in accordance with FED. R. CIV. P. 6(a) and (d)"; FRCP 6(a) governs
// "any local rule"). Agreed extensions of briefing time, the notice of
// each, and the motion for an opposed extension within the fourteen-day
// period are D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.4(a); a surreply needs leave (7.4(b)); the
// movant files a notice of completion of briefing (7.4(e)). Failing to
// file a response in time is consent to grant the motion, and failing to
// file a reply is consent that briefing is complete (7.1(b)). Objections
// to a pre-trial magistrate judge's non-dispositive ruling follow 7.3,
// 7.4 and 7.5 (72.1), so they take the motion periods and limits below.
// Rules that state no period or limit stay out: the writing and conferral
// requirement (7.1(a)), unopposed motions (7.2), the form of a motion
// (7.3), oral argument (7.6), summary judgment procedure, whose filing
// deadline is the scheduling order's (56.1), the duty to respond to
// discovery in the time a compelling order sets (37.2), continuances
// (40.1) and the Tenth Circuit appeal from a consent magistrate judge
// (73.3). All exhibits to a motion, response or reply are limited to a
// total of fifty pages unless all parties agree (10.5); no event carries
// exhibits alone, so that limit stays in this note. Page limits also stay
// in this note, because the rule states them as "double-spaced pages",
// which the limit check cannot match: a motion, or a motion and its
// supporting brief combined, is at most twenty-seven (27) double-spaced
// pages, a response twenty-four (24) and a reply twelve (12); unless
// otherwise ordered they apply to non-motion briefs too (7.5). The
// earlier D.N.M. outline's FRCP flow and its decisions (Twombly, Iqbal,
// and the Tenth Circuit's Robbins v. Oklahoma, 519 F.3d 1242) are FRCP
// authority and belong to lit/frcp; they are removed here: no reporter
// text is vendored.
/// The body of a Notice of Supplemental Authorities, and any response to
/// it: at most 350 words; no reply is permitted (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.8(c)).
limit supplemental-authorities {
  words <= 350 cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.8(c)"
} cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.8(c)"

/// A motion is served and filed (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.4(a)).
event MotionFiled()
/// A response to a motion is served and filed (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.4(a)).
event ResponseFiled()
/// A reply on a motion is served and filed (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.4(a)).
event ReplyFiled()
/// A Notice of Supplemental Authorities is filed (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.8).
event SupplementalAuthoritiesNoticeFiled() paper supplemental-authorities
/// A response to a Notice of Supplemental Authorities is filed
/// (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.8(c)).
event SupplementalAuthoritiesResponseFiled() paper supplemental-authorities
/// The Clerk gives notice that a filed paper lacks a signature
/// (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 10.3(b)).
event SignatureOmissionNoticed()
/// The Clerk gives written notice of a deficiency in a non-conforming
/// document (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 10.3(c)).
event DeficiencyNoticed()
/// The scheduling conference is held (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 16.1).
event SchedulingConference()
/// An objection to an interrogatory, request for production or
/// inspection, or request for admission is served (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 26.6).
event DiscoveryObjectionServed()
/// The scheduled deposition is taken (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 30.1).
event DepositionScheduled()
/// The Clerk gives written notice that an action with no steps taken for
/// ninety days may be dismissed (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 41.1).
event ProsecutionNoticeGiven()
/// Judgment is entered (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 54.1, 54.5(a)).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// A prevailing party's proposed order or judgment is served on each
/// party (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 58.2(a)).
event ProposedOrderServed()
/// A notice of removal is filed (D.N.M.LR-Civ. 81.1(a)).
event NoticeOfRemovalFiled()

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.4(a): a response is served and filed within fourteen
/// calendar days after service of the motion; the period may be extended
/// by agreement of all parties.
deadline response-period: 14.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.4(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.4(a): a reply is served and filed within fourteen
/// calendar days after service of the response.
deadline reply-period: 14.days after ResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.4(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.8(c): any response to a Notice of Supplemental
/// Authorities is filed within seven days of the filing of the Notice.
deadline supplemental-authorities-response-period: 7.days after SupplementalAuthoritiesNoticeFiled() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 7.8(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 10.3(b): a paper filed without signature is stricken
/// unless signed within fourteen days after the omission is called to the
/// party's attention.
deadline signature-cure-period: 14.days after SignatureOmissionNoticed() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 10.3(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 10.3(c): failure to remedy a deficiency, or show good
/// cause for non-compliance, within forty-five days from the date of the
/// Clerk's notice may result in striking or dismissal without prejudice
/// under D.N.M.LR-Civ. 41.2.
deadline deficiency-cure-period: 45.days after DeficiencyNoticed() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 10.3(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 16.1: after the FRCP 26(f) conference the parties file
/// the completed Joint Status Report at least seven days before the
/// scheduling conference, or as ordered by the Court.
deadline joint-status-report-period: 7.days before SchedulingConference() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 16.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 26.6: a party served with an objection to an
/// interrogatory, request for production or inspection, or request for
/// admission proceeds under D.N.M.LR-Civ. 37.1 within twenty-one days of
/// service of the objection (or, where the response says documents will
/// be produced, of the production or inspection); failure to proceed in
/// time is acceptance of the objection. The Court may change the period
/// for good cause.
deadline discovery-objection-motion-period: 21.days after DiscoveryObjectionServed() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 26.6"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 30.1: notice of a deposition under FRCP 30(b) is served
/// at least fourteen days before the scheduled deposition, unless the
/// parties agree or the Court orders a shorter time.
deadline deposition-notice-period: 14.days before DepositionScheduled() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 30.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 41.1: a civil action in which no steps are taken for
/// ninety days may be dismissed thirty days after the date of the Clerk's
/// written notice, unless good cause is shown.
deadline want-of-prosecution-period: 30.days after ProsecutionNoticeGiven() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 41.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 54.1: a motion to tax costs is filed and served within
/// thirty days of entry of judgment; failure to do so waives the claim to
/// costs.
deadline costs-motion-period: 30.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 54.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 54.5(a): a motion for attorney's fees not brought under
/// 28 U.S.C. § 2412(d) is filed and served within thirty days after entry
/// of judgment; failure to do so waives the claim to fees.
deadline fee-motion-period: 30.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 54.5(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 58.2(a)(2): a prevailing party's proposed order or
/// judgment is entered if not objected to within seven days of service.
deadline proposed-order-objection-period: 7.days after ProposedOrderServed() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 58.2(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// D.N.M.LR-Civ. 81.1(a): a party removing an action under 28 U.S.C.
/// § 1446 files legible copies of the state-court records and proceedings
/// within twenty-eight days after filing the notice of removal.
deadline removal-record-period: 28.days after NoticeOfRemovalFiled() counted_by frcp6-new-mexico cite "D.N.M.LR-Civ. 81.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}
